## SystemOnTPTP

`SystemOnTPTP` needs no credentials — the cell ships ready to pick a prover
from the live-fetched list and run it.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJiYWNrZW5kIjoiaXNhYmVsbGUiLCJwcm9ibGVtX3N0ciI6InRoZih0ZXN0LCBjb25qZWN0dXJlLCAkdHJ1ZSA9PiAkZmFsc2UpLiIsInByb29mX21ldGhvZCI6InNsZWRnZWhhbW1lciBuaXRwaWNrIG5pdHBpY2tbc2F0aXNmeV0gb29wcyIsInN5c3RlbSI6IkFsdC1FcmdvLS0tMC45NS4yIiwidGhlbWUiOiJEcmFjdWxhIiwidGltZV9saW1pdCI6NSwidHB0cDR4X2VuYWJsZWQiOmZhbHNlfQ","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoAtpClient.AtpSolver","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
# Generated by ATP Solver (backend: Isabelle)
problem = "thf(test, conjecture, $true => $false)."

# Uses the auto-managed local Isabelle server when `isabelle` is on PATH,
# otherwise falls back to AtpClient.Isabelle's remote-config path.
case KinoAtpClient.IsabelleRuntime.available?() do
  :ok -> KinoAtpClient.IsabelleRuntime.query_tptp(problem, proof_method: "sledgehammer nitpick nitpick[satisfy] oops")
  {:error, _} -> AtpClient.Isabelle.query_tptp(problem, proof_method: "sledgehammer nitpick nitpick[satisfy] oops")
end

```

## Other backends

Switch the backend dropdown to `StarExec`, `Isabelle`, or `LocalExec`. The
header controls and the result panel adapt automatically: StarExec and
LocalExec normalize their output to a single SZS-status badge, while Isabelle
expands into a per-lemma table with the result of each generated lemma.
